{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"artifacthub/community-operators/kubero-operator","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:16:59.734Z","source":{"name":"Artifact Hub","api":"https://artifacthub.io/api/v1/packages/olm/community-operators/kubero-operator","page":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/olm/community-operators/kubero-operator"},"readme":"Kubero is a Internal Developer Platform (IDP) that brings the convinience of Heroku/platform.sh/vercel/Netlify to your kubernetes cluster. Your developers should not need to worry about the underlying infrastructure and deployment. It enables you to deploy your applications with a few clicks. It also provides a API and CLI to manage your applications.\n\n## Features\n- Automated GitOps deployment and Pull Request previews\n- Integrated CI/CD\n\n## Supported Git Providers\n- Gitea\n- Forgejo (WIP)\n- OneDev (WIP)\n- Gogs\n- Github\n- Gitlab\n- Bitbucket\n\n## Tested languages/frameworks\nBasicly everything that can be shipped in a single container. Kubero uses official images to build and run the apps. But they can be replaced or extended to fit your needs.\n\n- GoLang (including Hugo, gin-gonic)\n- Python (including Flask)\n- JavaScript/NodeJS\n- PHP (including Laravel)\n- Ruby (including Rails)\n- Static HTML\n- Rust (including Rocket)","readmeBase":"https://github.com/k8s-operatorhub/community-operators/operators","publisher":{"name":"Operator Framework","url":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/search?org=operator-framework","official":false,"verified":false,"cncf":false},"registered":null,"updated":"2024-10-04T14:18:51.000Z","categories":["Integration and delivery"],"keywords":["gitops","devops","workflow","Integration & Delivery"],"license":null,"links":[{"name":"Kubero Operator","url":"https://github.com/kubero-dev/kubero-operator"},{"name":"Kubero UI","url":"https://github.com/kubero-dev/kubero"},{"name":"source","url":"https://github.com/kubero-dev/kubero"},{"name":"Community Operators repository","url":"https://github.com